# AI Handoff — data/

**Updated:** 2026-09-19  
**Active modeling doctrine:** fixed-target transductive reconstruction.

## Core contract

```text
ID_POLIGONO
RENDIMIENTO_T_HA
CONJUNTO
197 parcels
138 ENTRENAMIENTO
59 PREDICCION
target cycle: April–October 2025
states: Hidalgo, Puebla, Tlaxcala
```

The parcel is the supervised unit. BASIC/PRO rows are repeated parcel/date/sensor observations.

All 59 target covariate histories are observable and are legitimate inputs to X-only
transductive modeling. Their hidden FIRA yields are not observable.

## Official longitudinal sources

```text
BASIC: 107,666 × 96; 197 parcels; 2022–2025; Sentinel-2 + Landsat;
       23 index families × promedio/std/max/min.
PRO:    47,804 × 20; 197 parcels; 2025; Planet;
       NDVI/EVI/LAI/MSAVI × promedio/std/max/min.
```

Preserve date and sensor provenance. Do not silently merge same-named indices across sensors.

## Canonical parcel-level products

```text
data/processed/features_v1/
  clean        197 × 699
  competition  197 × 1408
  all          197 × 1408

manifest: 694 clean + 709 competition-only = 1403 total features

data/processed/agronomic_features_v1/
  197 × 351 = ID + 350 derived features

data/processed/empirical_features_v1/
  197 × 336 = ID + 335 derived features
```

`competition` is the active feature mode. `clean` remains historical/provenance only.

Feature Table v1 is a useful compression, not the only modeling representation. Checkpoint 04
may use the original longitudinal BASIC/PRO trajectories directly.

## Transductive learning policy

For active Checkpoint 04:

- X-only representations may be learned jointly from labeled + target X;
- pseudo-competition validation must expose pseudo-target X while hiding pseudo-target y;
- any y-aware selection/search sees only the labeled portion of that pseudo-experiment;
- direct hidden-target access is forbidden.

This supersedes the older blanket rule that every learned X-only representation must be fitted
without seeing holdout X. That older rule remains part of the historical Checkpoint 03
inductive evaluation contract.

## External evidence already acquired

- INEGI municipal boundaries;
- CHIRPS daily 2025-04-01 through 2025-10-31;
- WaPOR AETI and NPP;
- SoilGrids: 9 properties × 4 depths;
- SIAP 2003–2025;
- high-resolution INEGI CEM for Hidalgo/Puebla/Tlaxcala;
- official climate/topography;
- ERA5-Land remains optional but is a candidate for richer daily weather/stress evidence.

## SIAP priority

SIAP 2025 is desirable contemporaneous evidence, not leakage from the hidden parcel target.
Re-audit the most specific valid municipal proxy for:

```text
Cebada grano
relevant agricultural cycle
Temporal modality
correct Estado/Municipio / CVEGEO
```

Keep `Cebada grano` separate from forage barley. Never join on municipality ID alone.

## QC caveats

- current CHIRPS Feature Table build retained only one daily competition feature; investigate extraction/aggregation before concluding CHIRPS is uninformative;
- preserve SoilGrids unit conversions and CRS rules;
- WaPOR totals use duration metadata;
- source files remain immutable.

## Current data task

Support Checkpoint 04A/04B by exposing parcel-level geometry plus reusable longitudinal
trajectories and by building target-vs-train similarity/support diagnostics without touching
the hidden 59 y values.
